 Horror, if you wanted to see it that way =)<br /> Otherwise, I don't think there is anything quite like it in the Flesh world, but you could see the Upside-Down as the Shadow rather easily, making the big thing (somethingsomethinghydra) a high-ranking spirit, I suppose. Maybe Will is in the process of being Claimed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T14:21:05-07:00","id":1129974,"title":"","content":"Upside Down does the &quot;dark reflection of our world quite well. If only all we seen it so far weren't so inimical of human life, I'd be tempted to translate it to the Shadow, but its fauna and flora seem to have a theme that does not coexist well with our world. Abyss, perhaps? Lower Depth that gets something by feeding on people and using them as incubators? Or just really bad corner of the Shadow?<br /> <br /> Questions, questions, questions...<br /> <br /> (That said, hype for season 2!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T01:43:51-07:00","id":1130174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1129836-stranger-things-season-2-trailer-posted-here-for-cofd-innocents-inspiration?p=1129974#post1129974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Upside Down does the &quot;dark reflection of our world quite well. If only all we seen it so far weren't so inimical of human life, I'd be tempted to translate it to the Shadow, but its fauna and flora seem to have a theme that does not coexist well with our world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Upside Down is Idigam spawn-ruled local Shadow Realm - if it acts like Shadow, feels like Shadow, but looks alien even for Shadow - it clearly is Idigam! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-17-2017, 05:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value"